<title>FRANCE: Paribas says signed Credit du Nord sale.</title>
<headline>Paribas says signed Credit du Nord sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Groupe Paribas said on Tuesday it completed talks and signed an agreement to sell its Credit du Nord banking unit to French bank Societe Generale.</p>
<p>The final sale price for 100 percent of the capital was fixed at 2.2 billion francs, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Under the deal, first announced in January, Societe Generale will initially hold 61.6 percent of Credit du Nord and will acquire the balance in the next three years.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
